      "lineNbr": 300,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T06:04:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "normally the way you check v4 checksum is by checking it is one\u0027s complement zero, which in practice means it should be 0xFFFF... ie. calculate the one\u0027s complement checksum of the entire ipv4 header - *including* the checksum field - fold it down to a u16 - check it is exactly the negative zero, ie. 0xFFFF (technically positive zero would be ok too, *but* it turns out that positive zero is impossible to achive for a non-all-zeroes buffer, due to how sum/fold work)",
      "parentUuid": "5a625c56_f7b927d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 300,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 300,
